    "body": "## Summary\n- expose the exact locally-expired job publication id without changing existing boolean expiry compatibility\n- after each scheduler-driven local expiry transaction completes, best-effort cancel the attached Stripe PaymentIntent\n- stop provider cleanup when no publication was expired and keep the existing 25-per-tick bound\n- add scheduler regression coverage proving local expiry happens before provider cleanup\n\n## Financial / security invariants\n- wallet reservation release and terminal local publication state remain authoritative\n- Stripe cleanup happens only after the local expiry call returns; provider failure cannot roll back ledger state\n- signed-webhook late-payment recovery remains authoritative for races where Stripe succeeds before cancellation reaches the provider\n- no client secret, job payload or private route/address data is exposed\n- no schema change / Flyway migration required\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all latest-head required CI/checks complete successfully. Any failure will be fixed on this branch and revalidated.",
